:::oak-task {id="task-b"}

:::oak-heading {id="task-b-heading" level="2"}
Task B: Why must everyone follow the law?
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="task-b-scenario" keep-with-next="true"}
A group of teenagers decide to cross a railway track instead of using the bridge because it is quicker. One of them says, “The rules don’t really matter if no-one is watching.”
:::

:::oak-question {id="question-2"}
Using the example above, explain why laws must always be followed.

:::oak-answer-space {id="question-2-response" kind="lines" lines="10"}
:::
:::
:::

:::oak-task {id="task-c"}

:::oak-heading {id="task-c-heading" level="2"}
Task C: What does fair treatment under the law mean?
:::

:::oak-paragraph {id="task-c-scenario" keep-with-next="true"}
A 16-year-old signs up for a gym membership, but later realises the terms and conditions were unclear. When they try to cancel, the company refuses, even though the key information wasn’t properly explained to them beforehand.
:::

:::oak-question {id="question-3"}
Explain whether this is fair and how the rule of law protects this young person.

Use the words ‘equality’ and ‘accountability’ in your answer.

:::oak-answer-space {id="question-3-response" kind="lines" lines="12"}
